# Enums — a fixed set of constants

## A closed, named set

```java
public enum Status { ACTIVE, SUSPENDED, CLOSED }
Status s = Status.ACTIVE;
```

The only instances that can exist — no fourth, no typo. Beats a `String` (`"activ"` slips through) or an `int` (`3` means nothing).

## Free methods

- **`values()`** — all constants, in order · **`valueOf("ACTIVE")`** — parse by name
- **`name()`** → `"ACTIVE"` · **`ordinal()`** → position (**don't persist it** — reordering shifts it)

## Exhaustive `switch`

```java
String label = switch (s) {
    case ACTIVE    -> "open";
    case SUSPENDED -> "on hold";
    case CLOSED    -> "shut down";
};   // no default — add a constant, compiler flags this
```

**Collections:** `EnumSet` / `EnumMap` — faster than `HashSet`/`HashMap` for enum keys.
